Monday Update
* Trade Alert: Half of XOM and CAT calls sold for big gain; buy AMAT calls*=
 Stocks steam ahead amid rising expectation of fiscal stimulus package in D=
C*Stocks are higher midday in synch with crude oil prices after Treasury Se=
cretary Janet Yellen reiterated that aggressive US fiscal stimulus was need=
ed to support the labor market.The Dow Jones Industrial Average rose 0.5% w=
ith the S&amp;P 500 higher by 0.4% and the Nasdaq Composite higher by 0.6%.=
 Energy was the standout gainer, followed by materials, while utilities was=
 the steepest decliner after midday on Monday.West Texas Intermediate oil f=
utures climbed by 2.1% to $58.06 and gold jumped by $23.4 per troy ounce to=
 $1,836.8 after the dollar weakened slighty.The US 10-year yield fell 1.2 b=
asis points to 1.15% intraday, retreating from an 11-month high on Friday w=
hen a disappointing 49,000 increase in US non-farm payrolls -- after 159,00=
0 of downward revisions to earlier months -- underpinned hopes for Presiden=
t Joe Biden's proposed $1.9 billion economic relief program.Citing Yellen's=
 weekend interviews, a note from Daiwa Capital said Monday that she that re=
iterated aggressive fiscal stimulus is warranted in light of the "stalling"=
 job growth in Friday's employment report.Portfolio:&nbsp;Our new XOM and C=
AT calls sold at first targets for gains of 30% and 39%, which is great. Ad=
just targets and stops. =E2=80=A6 We have one new idea for you.*CURRENT REC=
OMMENDATIONSExxon Mobil Corp. (XOM) February $45 calls-- Symbol: XOM210219C=
00045000-- Filled at $5.00 on Friday Feb 5. -- Sold have today Feb 8 at $6.=
50 for 30% gain!-- Now trading at $7.10-- Set up to sell second half at $8.=
